   "source": [
    "# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) \u2014 Real-World Resume & Job Description Dataset\n",
    "## Course: AI & Machine Learning | 2nd Year Project\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook conducts a complete Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on real-world applicant resumes (`.docx`, `.txt`) across three technical career domains:\n",
    "1. **Java & J2EE / Full-Stack Engineering**\n",
    "2. **IT Business Analysis & Agile Scrum**\n",
    "3. **Backend Python Engineering**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Import Libraries and Load Data Loader"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import re\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import data_loader\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"All libraries imported successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Ingest Real Candidate Resumes from `sample_data/`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sample_dir = \"sample_data\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find all candidate resumes\n",
    "files = [f for f in sorted(os.listdir(sample_dir)) \n",
    "         if f.lower().endswith(('.docx', '.txt')) \n",
    "         and not f.startswith('job_description') \n",
    "         and not f.startswith('test_empty')]\n",
    "\n",
    "corpus = []\n",
    "for f in files:\n",
    "    path = os.path.join(sample_dir, f)\n",
    "    text = data_loader.load_text_from_file(path)\n",
    "    words = re.findall(r'\\b[a-zA-Z]{2,}\\b', text.lower())\n",
    "    corpus.append({\n",
    "        \"filename\": f,\n",
    "        \"char_count\": len(text),\n",
    "        \"word_count\": len(words),\n",
    "        \"unique_words\": len(set(words)),\n",
    "        \"lexical_diversity\": round(len(set(words)) / len(words), 4) if words else 0,\n",
    "        \"words\": words,\n",
    "        \"text\": text\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully ingested {len(corpus)} applicant documents.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Document Length & Lexical Diversity Table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_stats = pd.DataFrame([{\n",
    "    \"Resume Document\": c[\"filename\"],\n",
    "    \"Total Characters\": c[\"char_count\"],\n",
    "    \"Total Words\": c[\"word_count\"],\n",
    "    \"Unique Words\": c[\"unique_words\"],\n",
    "    \"Lexical Diversity\": c[\"lexical_diversity\"]\n",
    "} for c in corpus])\n",
    "\n",
    "df_stats"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Visualizing Document Length Distribution\n",
    "Demonstrating the massive variance between concise summaries (~100 words) and multi-page dossiers (up to 6,300+ words)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "clean_names = [c[\"filename\"].replace('.docx', '').replace('.DOCX', '').replace('.txt', '')[:16] for c in corpus]\n",
    "word_counts = [c[\"word_count\"] for c in corpus]\n",
    "\n",
    "bars = plt.barh(clean_names, word_counts, color=\"#3498db\", edgecolor=\"#2980b9\", height=0.65)\n",
    "plt.title(\"EDA: Candidate Resume Word Count Distribution\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=12)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Word Count\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Candidate Profile\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    w = bar.get_width()\n",
    "    plt.text(w + 50, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2, f\"{int(w):,}\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8.5, color=\"#2c3e50\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.xlim(0, max(word_counts) * 1.15)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5: Technical Skill Term Frequency Analysis\n",
    "Extracting occurrences of key technical competencies across the candidates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tracked_skills = [\"python\", \"java\", \"spring\", \"aws\", \"sql\", \"docker\", \"agile\", \"scrum\", \"microservices\", \"hadoop\", \"spark\", \"jira\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "skill_records = []\n",
    "for c in corpus:\n",
    "    counts = Counter(c[\"words\"])\n",
    "    row = {s: counts[s] for s in tracked_skills}\n",
    "    row[\"Candidate\"] = c[\"filename\"].replace('.docx', '').replace('.DOCX', '').replace('.txt', '')[:16]\n",
    "    skill_records.append(row)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_skills = pd.DataFrame(skill_records).set_index(\"Candidate\")\n",
    "df_skills"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 6: Technical Competencies Heatmap\n",
    "Visualizing the domain clusters: Java Engineers, Business Analysts, and Big Data Developers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(11, 6))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(df_skills, cmap=\"YlGnBu\", annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cbar=True, linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "plt.title(\"EDA: Technical Skill Term Frequency Heatmap\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=12)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Technical Skills\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Candidate Profile\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 7: Key EDA Findings for Project Report & PPT\n",
    "1. **Document Length Variance**: Real resumes range from 14 words (test stub) and 102 words (concise summary) to 6,332 words (Priya B.docx, 9 pages).\n",
    "2. **Lexical Richness vs. Length**: As resume length expands with redundant project descriptions, lexical diversity drops from ~80% down to 13%.\n",
    "3. **Domain Clustering**:\n",
    "   - **Java/Spring Cluster**: Priya (77 Java / 93 Spring), sai k (45/45), Sai Srinivas (40/18), Varun (31/58), Vishnu (22/22).\n",
    "   - **Business Analysis Cluster**: Vikash & Teresa (dominant in Scrum, Agile, Jira, and BRDs).\n",
    "   - **Big Data Cluster**: Vijay Bhargav (Hadoop: 26, Spark: 24).\n",
    "   - **Backend Python Cluster**: resume.txt (FastAPI, Python backend)."
   ]
  }
 ]
}